It reproduces the public API of Unsloth (names and arguments of
FastLanguageModel and FastModel) so that code written for Unsloth runs with
it. It contains no code from Unsloth. Unsloth is a trademark of its owners;
meepsquared is not affiliated with or endorsed by them.

It includes the LoRA kernels of Axolotl (https://github.com/axolotl-ai-cloud/axolotl),
v0.21.0, Apache License 2.0, in src/meepsquared/_vendor/axolotl/, with the changes
listed in the README there. Axolotl's kernel module credits Unsloth for the
inspiration of these kernels.

At run time it uses, without copying their code:
- Transformers, PEFT, TRL and Accelerate (Hugging Face, Apache License 2.0)
- Liger Kernel (LinkedIn, BSD 2-Clause License)
- bitsandbytes (MIT License), for QLoRA
- FlashAttention (BSD 3-Clause License), when installed
